                <pb facs="0563" n="475" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg475"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Don Luis Cadarso</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >governor of the Eastern Caroline Islands.</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">I do hereby give notice:</hi></p>
                <p>According news that I have received for the schooner <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fowler</hi>, will arrive very soon the military expedition, and I recommend
                    to all the chiefs of Metalamin tribe, to accomplish in the term of four days,
                    the following conditions, in order that all the tribe should not be destroyed: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>To deliver all the arms and munitions of the tribe.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Presentation to the government house, of the Chiefs Rogin Metalamin,
                            Krouni-letau in Tapalau, Manliam, Nanpue in Kiuakap, Taulik, Taul,
                            Nauchas, Re-rim, Namalie and Marrekiulau, in order to do their
                            discharges.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>To begin to gather good woods, to continue the built of the fort when
                            the troops arrive.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>St. James (Ponape)</placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1890-08-28">August 28,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/> The governor,<lb/>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal.</hi>] <signed><hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Luis Cadarso.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
